WEBVTT

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:08.440
Where are you going, Mizuto-kun?

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.820
Right back at you. Where are
 <i>you</i> going, Yume-san?

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.660
Oh? I thought you two were headed out.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.730
We were just about to leave.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:22.840
For that bookstore 
on Karasuma Street, by chance?

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.800
A little bird told me you like to read!

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.400
So you two must be headed to the same place.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.800
Yume only ever goes to the
 bookstore or the library, after all.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.260
M-Mom, please!

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.470
I trust you'll take care of her, Mizuto-kun.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:40.390
S-Sure thing...

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:43.390
All righty then. You two get along, okay?

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.540
Take care!

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.670
Why did you say yes?

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.780
You heard her. 
She didn't give me much choice.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:58.490
Why should I have to tag along
 with someone like you?

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:03.000
Whatever. I don't want you
 tagging along, either.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.810
I always hated how passive you are.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:07.960
Stupid geek!

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:11.720
And I always hated how selfish <i>you</i> are.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:12.960
Stupid nerd!

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.470
<b>Irido</b>

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:22.740
That curry was so good!

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:26.310
<b>The Former Couple Refuses to Say...</b>

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:26.310
<b>"It's things like this...!"</b>

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:24.920
I'm glad you liked it.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.190
Thanks for the meal.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:29.060
Of course!

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:35.570
Thanks for the meal.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.050
I'm so glad they seem to be getting along.

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:44.560
You're telling me.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:47.460
To suddenly get a housemate
of the opposite sex at that age...

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:51.610
I guess that sort of thing 
doesn't matter much nowadays.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.340
Well, looks like I was worried over nothing!

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:58.960
Families come in all shapes 
and sizes these days.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:01.670
Just because they're stepsiblings 
doesn't mean they can't get along.

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:03.720
Here you go, dear.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.680
You get it, don't you?

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.230
Why thank you, Yuni-san.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:06.920
Get what?

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:10.770
We mustn't do anything to upset them.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.350
I know that.

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:15.980
I'll take what happened 
between us to my grave.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:17.240
Excellent.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.200
Look who's all high and mighty.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.260
Since when were you this bossy?

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.290
If I wasn't like this before,

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:28.170
then it's certainly your fault 
that I'm like this now.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.250
Huh?

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:30.790
Got a problem?

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.960
Apparently their daughter's 
gonna start living on her own.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:34.430
Yeah?

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:35.380
Yeah, and I heard...

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.310
<b>Beyond All Limits</b>

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.320
I've completely reached my limit.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:57.320
<b>Something's Wrong...</b>

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:56.840
Is something wrong?

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:04.110
How much longer do you plan on calling 
me by my given name like it's nothing?

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:08.510
You're using my given name too.

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:10.960
That's better than you using mine.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:14.280
Not much we can do now
 that we share a family name.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.340
What would you suggest I call you?

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:19.290
That's obvious, isn't it? It's perfect.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:20.970
What is?

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:22.720
"Onee-chan."

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.470
Huh?

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:31.190
We're siblings now, so addressing me
as your older sister makes perfect sense, no?

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:33.100
Hold it, hold it, hold it.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:36.630
<i>You're</i> the older sibling?

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.850
Gimme a break. It's the other way around.

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:42.360
<i>I'm</i> the older sibling here.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:47.920
Let me put this simply, since your 
brain cells seem to be off duty right now.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.500
Listen well.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:55.130
Our society considers the 
firstborn child to be the eldest.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:57.720
That's premise number one.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:03.040
I was born before you. 
That's premise number two.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.010
Therefore, I am the older sibling.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.930
It's the logical conclusion. You follow?

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:14.180
But if memory serves, weren't we 
both born on November 3rd?

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:16.730
So we're the same age, correct?

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:20.120
By the day, perhaps,
 but that's not everything.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.630
You must also consider the time of birth.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.950
Time of birth?

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:28.700
I asked Mineaki-san in order
 to settle the matter.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:32.410
I was born at 11:04 AM,

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:37.970
while <i>you</i> were born at 11:34 AM.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.460
In other words, I was born
 thirty minutes earlier.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:44.810
You with me?

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:51.960
Didn't Japan used to consider the firstborn
 twin to be younger in ancient times?

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.660
But we're not twins.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.760
We're not even siblings in the first place.

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:01.500
Hey, wait a second...

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.950
We consider the firstborn 
to be the eldest now anyway.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:08.200
Just go along with it, would you?

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.090
Thought you could fool me?

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:13.480
Whatever. I'm the older sibling. QED.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.460
Case dismissed.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.400
<i>I'm</i> going to be the older sibling.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.920
The thought of being your 
little sister creeps me out!

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.120
Same here!

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.670
I'd take anything over 
being your little brother!

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:32.140
Wait, hang on.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.230
What?

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:35.700
Glaring at each other won't get us anywhere.

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:41.400
At times like this, any reasonable person
 would settle things with a game.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.690
Irritating choice of words, but you're right.

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:47.780
In that case...

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:49.740
How about this?

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:52.270
We've both accepted the fact that

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:54.120
we'll have to hide our previous relationship

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:58.170
and act like any normal stepsiblings would.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:01.130
We've both been doing well so far,

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:04.140
but either one of us may yet slip up

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:06.410
and do something out of line, no?

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:09.390
So whoever screws up first loses.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.920
So whoever first acts in a manner 
unnatural for a stepsibling

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:13.120
<b>Little Brother</b>

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:16.330
becomes the younger brother or sister?

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:14.140
<b>Little Sister</b>

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.620
<b>Little Brother</b>

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.620
<b>Little Sister</b>

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.680
The sense of competition 
engendered by such a rule

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.900
should also help inspire us 
to better hide our past.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:27.920
So do these rules apply even 
when our parents aren't around?

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:28.910
Of course.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:33.400
Also, that's per slip-up.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:38.210
The winner gets to decide how the 
younger shows it every time.

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:42.120
I guess there'd be no point 
if it was sudden death.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:43.840
Okay, let's go with that.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:45.590
Then...

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.300
The game starts now.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.430
Wai—What are you doing?!

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:59.310
Oh, what's wrong? 
Isn't this normal sibling behavior?

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:02.440
<i>I get it now...</i>

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:09.910
<i>It seems he's finally realized the true 
nature of the rules I laid out..</i>

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:11.900
<i>Even if it's an obvious provocation,</i>

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:15.020
<i>I'm not allowed to show 
irritation over any action</i>

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:19.110
<i>that would be considered
 normal among siblings.</i>

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:23.600
<i>Such a reaction would fall into the 
category of "unnatural for a stepsibling."</i>

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:24.750
<i>In other words...</i>

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:27.740
<i>This was just a ploy to get under my skin!</i>

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:32.490
<i>Stupid girl... She proposed 
those rules just for that?!</i>

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:35.030
<i>She's twisted!</i>

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:37.810
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:42.460
<i>My own personal Pandora's box is right there!</i>

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:46.010
<i>That drawer contains things
I can't let anyone see!</i>

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:54.950
<i>What do I do? What do I do?
What do I do? What do I do?!</i>

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.040
Forgive me...

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:05.790
I can't bear to fight with you any longer.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:08.330
If I've upset you, I apologize.

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:09.910
I'll even get out of your sight.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:13.550
So please...

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:17.260
Can we put this behind us?

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:25.260
Irido-kun...

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.830
Yup, you're out!

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:33.070
Siblings don't call each 
other by their last names.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.740
B-But you're out too, aren't you?

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:45.500
Wanting to bury the hatchet is completely 
normal for siblings, don't you think?

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:51.000
Now then, since this is the first round, 
let's keep it simple.

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:53.510
Just say it.

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:56.010
H-How should I say it?

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:58.260
However you'd like.

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:13.780
O-Onii-chan...

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:20.580
Well, you've learned your lesson.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:23.800
Now you know not to mess with me.

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:28.300
You may fancy yourself a
 hardcore mystery fan,

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:31.530
but you and I simply aren't
on the same level up here.

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:34.090
You never...

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:37.030
used to be this mean to me back then!

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:41.850
There, there.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:45.100
You're right. I'm sorry.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.440
Onee...

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:49.190
Nee-san.

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:52.190
Th-This is the part of you I...

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:56.240
I always hated how you flip-flop like that!

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.700
Stupid Onii-chan!

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:08.140
You both look wonderful!

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:08.870
<b>Rakuro High School
Entrance 
Ceremony</b>

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:14.380
<b>Rakuro High School
Entrance Ceremony</b>

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:11.480
<i>It would've been one thing...</i>

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:14.020
<i>...if we were only going to the same school.</i>

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:17.380
Squeeze in closer, you two.

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:23.810
<b>New Students\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hClass Assignments</b>

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:23.810
Student Name

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:23.810
Pronunciation

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:21.850
<i>But we're in the same class.</i>

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:23.810
<i>With the same surname.</i>

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:26.430
<i>I guess pretending to be strangers...</i>

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.480
Say cheese!

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:31.820
<i>...is kind of out of the question now.</i>

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:37.820
Rakuro High School Entrance Ceremony

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:41.770
We're walking to school separately 
starting tomorrow, got it?

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.820
That goes without saying.

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:49.230
Anyway, shouldn't you be more
 focused on making friends?

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:50.330
This is your high school debut.

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:52.710
My high school debut?

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:58.360
I'm the only one in the entire school 
who knows you used to be a total nerd.

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:00.930
It's the perfect time to reinvent yourself.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:04.010
Don't you worry, Mizuto-kun.

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:07.530
I have a secret weapon up my sleeve.

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:15.320
Rakuro High School Entrance Ceremony

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:09.850
<i>Now for the opening address.</i>

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:14.340
<i>Rakuro Private High School's 
entrance ceremony is about to begin.</i>

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:22.700
You were so cool back there, Irido-san!

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:24.830
You didn't seem nervous at all!

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:29.080
That's not true. I was a 
nervous wreck on the inside.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:30.360
Really?!

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:31.220
Yup.

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:33.080
<i>You little...</i>

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:38.420
Rakuro High School Entrance Ceremony

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:36.960
<i>And now a word from 
our first-year representative,</i>

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.420
<i>Irido Yume-san.</i>

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:40.420
Coming!

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:43.430
Lured by the warmth of the spring breeze,

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:46.430
the cherry blossoms start 
to bloom on this...

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:52.010
You must have aced the entrance exam
 if they made you the student rep, right?

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:54.110
How much did you study?

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:57.690
Not much... is what I'd like to say,

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:59.920
but honestly, I studied day and night.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:02.010
I still don't feel like 
I'm truly free from it.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:07.170
<i>How on earth does this girl 
have better grades than me?!</i>

00:12:07.170 --> 00:12:08.330
<i>You little...</i>

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.830
<i>Attendance</i>

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:11.830
Take your seats, everyone.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:14.580
Orientation

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:14.580
I'm gonna start orientation.

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:19.880
Irido!

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:23.800
What junior high did you go to?

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:26.980
Nagimi Middle. Why?

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:30.140
Huh. You play video games?

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:31.850
No, not really.

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:32.890
Gotcha.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:33.800
<i>Wh-What's going on?</i>

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:35.530
Just thought it might be fun 
to play together if you did.

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:35.800
<i>Why are people flocking to </i>me<i> now?</i>

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:37.230
Um...

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:38.940
So anyway...

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:42.690
Is it true you and Irido-san are stepsiblings?

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:49.950
<i>They really caught me off guard with that.</i>

00:12:50.840 --> 00:12:52.760
<i>But that girl...</i>

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:56.200
<i>Did she really tell everyone
 we're stepsiblings?</i>

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:58.330
<i>Even if they would've 
figured it out anyway...</i>

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:00.210
You know that Irido-san girl?

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:01.930
She's a real cutie, isn't she?

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:02.880
Yeah.

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:05.650
<i>A cutie? Give me a break.</i>

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:09.760
<i>I'd go to the optometrist and get 
my eyes checked if I were you.</i>

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:12.320
It was love at first sight.

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:15.520
So your plan is to get close 
with the younger brother, right?

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:19.130
If I went to her directly, 
she'd just shoot me down.

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:19.770
<i>So she told people I'm younger, huh? 
That girl...</i>

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:22.820
It'll be smooth sailing if I can get 
to her through him, y'know?

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:27.240
But her brother was such a killjoy.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.260
Maybe he just thought 
you were annoying?

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:30.740
Whoa, harsh!

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.650
<i>I see what's happening.</i>

00:13:32.650 --> 00:13:39.000
<i>So they mean to use me as a 
stepping stone to get to her, huh?</i>

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:41.000
<b>Irido</b>

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:53.810
What do you want?

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:57.440
Aren't you upset?

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:59.310
They're looking down on you.

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:02.320
You mean those guys that swarmed me?

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:05.840
They don't have the guts 
to speak to me directly,

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:09.160
but they assume <i>you're</i> a pushover, 
so they're using you to get to me.

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:12.080
I hate people like that.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:15.820
Don't let it bother you. 
They're not worth the time.

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:18.460
But then you'll—

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:20.300
What about me?

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:25.470
Nothing...

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:26.470
I see.

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:35.970
<b>My Stepmom's Daughter is my Ex</b>

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:44.920
<i>What is she doing?</i>

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:50.410
Hey...

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:51.570
What is it?

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:57.080
Didn't we agree to walk 
to school separately?

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:00.140
<i>What on earth is she thinking?</i>

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.790
Rakuro Private High School

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:06.990
Hey! It's Mizuto-kun.

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:08.270
Let's hang out.

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:09.590
Oh?

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.260
Sorry, you two.

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:16.330
Mizuto and I are talking right now,

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:18.640
so would you mind not getting in our way?

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:20.360
Irido-san...?

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:22.160
Y-You two aren't—

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:25.650
You <i>are</i> brother and sister, right?

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:26.650
Indeed.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:29.900
Sorry for having a brother complex.

00:15:35.090 --> 00:15:36.620
What was that?

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:38.730
Just now...

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:41.620
<b>Irido</b>

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:46.630
I'm gonna buy it and come home

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:46.630
Mom

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:46.630
Mom

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:46.630
Today

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:46.630
Sorry, Yume. I think I'm gonna be home late today. It seems like 
Mineaki-san is gonna be late too, so tell Mizuto-kun for me, will you?

00:15:44.390 --> 00:15:48.890
Looks like Mom and Mineaki-san 
will be home late tonight.

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:51.510
Should I make something to eat, then?

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:53.840
You can cook?

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:55.600
A little.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:58.120
It was just me and my dad, after all.

00:15:58.650 --> 00:15:59.850
And you...

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:02.810
You're terrible at it, right?

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:09.680
Well, what are you gonna make?

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:13.070
I'll see what's in the fridge 
and decide from there.

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:16.320
Okay, what do we have?

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:20.330
Eggs and fish... That'll need prepping.

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:22.710
What else?

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:24.500
Breasts, huh?

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.060
B-Breasts?!

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:26.750
Hmm?

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.800
Got something against chicken breast?

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:31.610
Oh... No, not really.

00:16:36.770 --> 00:16:37.470
Hey...

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:39.820
Hmm? What is it?

00:16:39.820 --> 00:16:42.430
About this morning...

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:45.190
The sensation... on your arm...

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:47.940
from when I hugged you...

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:50.900
You should wipe it from your memory!

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:51.910
Huh?

00:16:52.850 --> 00:16:57.660
Oh, yeah, I'd already forgotten about that.

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:00.290
I see!

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:06.510
Infuriating! So infuriating!

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:09.210
Absolutely, truly, and utterly infuriating!

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:15.470
You'd already forgotten, huh?

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:19.220
Are you trying to say mine are forgettable?

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:23.460
There must be some way

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:26.230
to break through his indifference...

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:35.860
<b>Japan Sinks</b>

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:41.100
I'm out now.

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:51.250
<i>All right! That worked better than I expected.</i>

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:53.760
I—You—What gives?!

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:57.760
I'm in my own home, you know?
It's not that big of a deal.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:01.640
No, but... I'm here, so...

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:03.520
Oh?

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:06.010
So what if my brother's here?

00:18:06.010 --> 00:18:07.270
Or, don't tell me...

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:12.330
Mizuto-kun, are you the kind of bad boy
who'd sneak a peek at his stepsister

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:14.400
with lusty eyes?

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:23.160
<i>He's getting redder by the second.</i>

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:26.680
<i>He turned away, but I can tell he's looking.</i>

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:31.000
<i>Guess I'll switch legs.</i>

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:37.300
<i>Ha, he looked! He definitely 
looked! So easy to read.</i>

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:41.000
<i>To think the guy who's always 
acting so cool-headed</i>

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:43.740
<i>would lose his composure like this.</i>

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:54.360
<i>O-Oh no! It's gonna... It's...</i>

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.510
<i>H-He's gonna see!</i>

00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:57.940
<i>Huh, wait.</i>

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:05.490
<i>Hold on a sec. It looks like I'm 
trying to seduce him, doesn't it?!</i>

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:09.260
<i>I think I got too carried away!</i>

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:11.250
<b>Japan Sinks</b>

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:24.150
W-Wait...

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:41.370
I know you were just trying to mess with me,

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:44.280
but didn't you realize this might happen?

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:47.070
You're usually so reserved,

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:50.830
but every now and then, you go and 
do something outrageous, don't you?

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:52.720
Like this morning.

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:54.680
If you act like that at school,

00:19:54.680 --> 00:19:57.550
you're gonna lose the reputation 
you've made for yourself.

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:02.050
But... you're family now.

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:06.250
I can't stand people looking 
down on my family like that!

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:15.560
Thanks. I appreciate it.

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:19.760
Don't you have something to say?

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:22.420
I genuinely thanked you, didn't I?

00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:24.460
D-Don't mention it!

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:26.320
I'm gonna go get in my pajamas—

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:32.160
<b>The Bottom of the Sea</b>

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:55.440
Ayai.

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:03.190
S-Stop... The rules...

00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:05.670
I don't mind

00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:08.200
losing today.

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:21.930
Mineaki-san, I'll hold the door, 
so would you be a dear and bring that in?

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:19.800
Wh-What do we do?!

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:20.760
Just hide!

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:22.190
Hide? But where?!

00:21:21.930 --> 00:21:23.210
Oh, sure!

00:21:22.190 --> 00:21:23.130
Uh...

00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:26.180
Is it all right if I leave 
everything in the corridor here?

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:27.080
Yeah.

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:27.930
Here!

00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:29.180
Huh?!

00:21:29.940 --> 00:21:31.980
We're home!

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:33.430
Oh? You alone, Mizuto?

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:36.140
Welcome home, Dad, Yuni-san.

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:38.220
Yume-san went to bed already.

00:21:38.220 --> 00:21:39.050
Oh, okay.

00:21:39.050 --> 00:21:42.090
Really? Aw, I brought back gifts.

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:45.650
<i>Just now, if our parents hadn't come home...</i>

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:50.470
<i>I was finally getting used 
to how things are.</i>

00:21:52.260 --> 00:21:55.750
<i>What was I thinking back there?</i>

00:21:57.460 --> 00:22:00.260
<i>I'd almost gotten over the past.</i>

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:03.210
<i>It's things like this...</i>

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:04.960
<i>It's things like this...</i>

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:07.430
<b>Irido</b>

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:06.760
<i>That I can't stand about him!</i>

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:06.760
<i>That I can't stand about her!</i>

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:21.360
<b>My Stepmom's 
Daughter is 
My Ex</b>
